---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import { companyInfo } from '@/lib/data';
---

<Layout
  title="Vaccine Policy — BenignBit"
  description="Read BenignBit's vaccine policy covering vaccinations, health guidelines and workplace safety measures for employees and visitors."
  keywords="vaccine policy, vaccination policy, BenignBit vaccine, workplace health"
  canonical="/vaccine-policy"
>
  <Header client:load />
  <main class="pt-28 md:pt-36">
    <article class="container-page max-w-3xl pb-20">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Vaccine Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: January 2025</p>

      <div class="prose-custom mt-8 space-y-6 text-muted-foreground">
        <p>BenignBit ("we", "us", "our") is committed to safeguarding the health and well-being of our employees, clients and the communities in which we operate. This policy outlines our approach to vaccinations and related workplace health measures.</p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Purpose</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">This policy is designed to reduce the spread of vaccine-preventable illnesses in our workplace, protect vulnerable individuals, and ensure a safe environment for in-person collaboration, client meetings and travel.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Scope</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">This policy applies to all employees, contractors, interns and visitors attending any BenignBit office or company-sponsored event. It is reviewed and updated in accordance with guidance from public health authorities.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Vaccination expectations</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>We strongly encourage all employees to stay up to date with vaccinations recommended by their local health authority, including seasonal influenza and COVID-19 boosters.</li>
            <li>Employees who are not vaccinated are encouraged to follow current public health guidance regarding masking and testing when working on-site.</li>
            <li>Proof of vaccination may be required for specific client engagements or travel where mandated by the client or destination country.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Medical and religious exemptions</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We respect individual health circumstances and beliefs. Employees may request an exemption from any vaccination requirement based on a documented medical condition or sincerely held religious belief. Requests should be submitted to Human Resources and will be reviewed on a case-by-case basis. Reasonable accommodations may include remote work arrangements, modified duties or enhanced safety protocols.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Workplace safety measures</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li>We maintain clean, well-ventilated office spaces and provide sanitization supplies at all workstations.</li>
            <li>Employees experiencing symptoms of a communicable illness are asked to work remotely and seek medical advice before returning on-site.</li>
            <li>We support flexible sick leave so employees can recover without pressure to come to the office.</li>
            <li>During periods of elevated public health risk, we may temporarily adjust on-site attendance, meeting formats or travel policies.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Privacy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Any vaccination information collected is treated as confidential health data. It is stored securely, access is restricted to authorized personnel only, and it is never shared externally without consent except where required by law.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Travel</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Employees traveling for company business must comply with the vaccination and health entry requirements of their destination. We will cover reasonable costs associated with required vaccinations for approved business travel.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Review and updates</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">This policy is reviewed at least annually and may be updated in response to new public health guidance. Employees will be notified of any material changes.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground">Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${companyInfo.email}`} class="text-primary hover:underline">{companyInfo.email}</a> or call {companyInfo.phone}.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
